{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310635,"nonce":"kHQstFJ/y1egSjDc91hjtV4j6aE=","title":"FIXED — `cast(class_obj, Interface)` double-wrapped, producing fat_ptr{fat_ptr, fn_ptr} where dispatch passed inner fat_ptr as `this`. Also ...","message":"`test_interface_cast` printed `draw:`/`click:` (empty `name` field) and `fail4` despite PASS exit code. Two distinct bugs.\n\n\n**Symptom**: `var g:I = cast(h, I); g.method()` — `this.field` reads as empty/garbage. Direct `var g:I = h` works.\n\n**Root cause**: `lower_expression` ([hir_to_mir.rs:7910-7944](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L7910)) post-processes class→interface promotion by wrapping. It calls `extract_underlying_class_symbol(expr)` to find the underlying class. For `Cast(Variable(h), I)` it RECURSED through the Cast and returned `h`'s class (Hello). The Cast handler had ALREADY produced a fat ptr via `wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr`; this second wrap allocated another fat ptr and stored the first fat_ptr's pointer as the \"object pointer\" at offset 0.\n\nMIR shape after the bug (excerpt):\n```\n$48 = malloc(16)                  ; first wrap (Cast handler)\nstore $48, $h_as_i64               ; obj_ptr = h\nstore $48+8, fn_ref @greet\n$54 = malloc(16)                  ; second wrap (lower_expression post-process)\nstore $54, $48 (as i64)            ; ← BUG: obj_ptr = fat_ptr_1, not h\nstore $54+8, fn_ref @greet\n```\n\nDispatch loaded obj_ptr from $54[0] = fat_ptr_1's address → called `greet(fat_ptr_1)` → inside greet, `this.who` was a GEP from the fat_ptr buffer → loaded the fn_ref slot → printed as empty string.\n\n**Fix** ([hir_to_mir.rs:32140](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L32140)): `extract_underlying_class_symbol` no longer recurses through `Cast { target, .. }` when target is an interface. The cast already wrapped — no underlying class remains to wrap.\n\n\n**Symptom**: `class Button extends Widget implements IClickable; class Widget implements IDrawable; cast(btn, IDrawable)` returned null, dropping the \"Button inherits IDrawable from Widget\" relationship.\n\n**Root cause**: `register_class_metadata`'s parent-vtable inheritance pass at [hir_to_mir.rs:34159](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L34159) resolved `parent_symbol` from `class.extends` ONLY via `type_table` — but `extends_canonical` synthetic TypeIds don't resolve there. Without `parent_symbol`, the inherited (Button, IDrawable) vtable was never built. Then the Cast handler's `interface_vtables.contains_key(\u0026(Button, IDrawable))` check at [hir_to_mir.rs:19127](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L19127) returned false and emitted `IrValue::Null`.\n\n**Fix**: Add the same SymbolId fallback (`SymbolId::from_raw(extends_type_id.as_raw())` + symbol-table lookup) here as in `class_parent_map.insert`. Now child classes inherit parent interface vtables across canonicalised extends.\n\n\n1. Whenever `lower_expression` may wrap a class as an interface, check that downstream consumers (cast handlers, Let init wrap, arg-boundary wrap) don't ALSO wrap the same value. The `init_is_safe_cast` skip in Let already covered Let; the post-process in `lower_expression` was the remaining hole.\n\n2. Any code path that pulls a class symbol from `class.extends` needs both type_table lookup AND `SymbolId::from_raw` fallback — see [[bugs-rtti-inheritance-walk]] for the matching `is_subclass_of` fix and the canonical pattern in `register_class_metadata`.\n\nVerification: 128/128 in `./run_haxe_tests.sh` and `test_interface_cast` now prints `draw:box / null / click:submit / button-draw:submit / done`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_interface_double_wrap` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}